      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, can you"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Noel J. Francisco (United States, amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER GENERAL FRANCISCO: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: If I could begin with Justice Kennedy's question. Justice Kennedy, we think that Ohio's process was permissible before Congress enacted the clarification amendment in 2002, but the clarification amendment made it even clearer for two basic reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: General, could you tell me, there's a 24-year history of solicitor generals of both political parties under both -- presidents of both political parties who have taken a position contrary to yours."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul M. Smith (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF PAUL M. SMITH ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS MR. SMITH: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I think it's important to recognize that the Supplemental Process violates Section 8 of the NVRA in two distinct ways. Of course, it violates the failure-to-vote clause, as we've been discussing, but it also violates 8(a) because 8(a) sets out an exclusive list of four bases that can be used for purging people from the rolls, and bars states from doing it under any other circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What?\nMR. SMITH: There are lists that are maintained by the federal government and the states. And they don't even defend this as a -- as a way to address that.\nJUSTICE BREYER: You know, I want to know what they are. I -- I am very ignorant in this field."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But are there -- are there statistics or -- is that just a commonsense argument, or are there statistics that show that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How do you get -- if \"by reason of a person's failure to vote\" is not but-for cause, how do you get around the language of (b)(2)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Now, that's what you've just said."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SMITH: The evidence we have in the record is that most people throw it in the wastebasket, 70 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "once you don't return the notice, you get put on the inactive list, correct?\nMR. SMITH: Right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: That means that you no longer -- does it mean you no longer get mailings about elections?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-980",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Except -- but it -- it goes on to say: \"except that no registrant may be removed solely by reason of failure to vote.\""
    },
